  "_skill_md": "---\nname: twitter\ndescription: Internal API for twitter\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://twitter.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Bearer Token\"\n  endpointCount: 20\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"social\"\n---\n\n# Twitter API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nBearer Token — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (1)\n- `POST /i/api/1.1/graphql/user_flow.json` — Initiate user authentication flow.\n\n### Data Read (14)\n- `GET /i/api/1.1/hashflags.json` — Fetch hashflags.\n- `GET /i/api/2/badge_count/badge_count.json` — Get badge counts.\n- `GET /i/api/fleets/v1/fleetline` — Fetch fleetline (stories).\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/-Afl9E3-pBgYsJ3jNUWV3Q/SidebarUserRecommendations` — Fetch sidebar user recommendations.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/8DJ2_AR5lFiA1BeiPoSzPw/useSubscriptionProductDetailsQuery` — Get subscription product details.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/dLyrLrPjasBJaw8lCQkXdA/ExploreSidebar` — Fetch explore sidebar content.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/I3V_Tt32aTZdw7cBdKUJbg/useStoryTopicQuery` — Get story topic information.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/kjTRZeD3JnAnLEdAkVNyxw/PinnedTimelines` — Fetch pinned timelines.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/nn16KxqX3E1OdE7WlHB5LA/HomeTimeline` — Fetch the home timeline.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/PFIxTk8owMoZgiMccP0r4g/getAltTextPromptPreference` — Get alt text prompt preference.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/SPJ9o9QzEK2l1Bh1vcgX6A/useFetchProductSubscriptionsQuery` — Fetch product subscriptions.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/xF6sXnKJfS2AOylzxRjf6A/DataSaverMode` — Get data saver mode settings.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/zCYojd6h_gVXYjFlaAk4bA/useDirectCallSetupQuery` — Query direct call setup.\n- `GET /i/api/graphql/zzeLdGlB0ZN6hiOYUIpDcQ/XChatDmSettingsQuery` — Get X Chat DM settings.\n\n### Data Write (2)\n- `POST /i/api/1.1/graphql/ces/p2` — Send data for CES P2.\n- `POST /i/api/1.1/graphql/error_log.json` — Log errors to Twitter.\n\n### Media (1)\n- `GET /sticky/animations/like.4.json` — Get like animation media.\n\n### Realtime (1)\n- `GET /live_pipeline/events` — Receive real-time events.\n\n### Config (1)\n- `GET /1.1/account/settings.json` — Get account settings.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"twitter\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /i/api/1.1/hashflags.json\" }\n```\n\nHere are a few quick start examples to get you going:\n\n```typescript\n// Fetch the user's home timeline.  This is a common read operation.\nasync function getHomeTimeline() {\n  try {\n    const timeline = await client.get_i_api_graphql_nn16KxqX3E1OdE7WlHB5LA_HomeTimeline();\n    console.log(\"Home Timeline:\", timeline);\n    return timeline;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching home timeline:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Log an error to Twitter.  This is a common write operation.\nasync function logError(errorMessage: string) {\n  try {\n    const response = await client.post_i_api_1_1_graphql_error_log_json({\n      message: errorMessage,\n      // Add other error details as needed\n    });\n    console.log(\"Error logged successfully:\", response);\n    return response;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error logging failed:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Fetch sidebar user recommendations.\nasync function getSidebarRecommendations() {\n  try {\n    const recommendations = await client.get_i_api_graphql__Afl9E3_pBgYsJ3jNUWV3Q_SidebarUserRecommendations();\n    console.log(\"Sidebar Recommendations:\", recommendations);\n    return recommendations;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching sidebar recommendations:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Bearer Token\n**Base URL:** `https://twitter.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 4 auth headers, 214 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Twitter's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Twitter data without official API access\n- Automate actions on twitter.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Twitter frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { TwitterClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await TwitterClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 4 (authorization, x-csrf-token, x-twitter-auth-type, x-guest-token)\n- **Session cookies:** 214\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (20)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
